<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e>
      a       zoo:Oeuvre ;
      zoo:author "NEMESIANUS, MARCUS AURELIUS OLYMPUS" ;
      zoo:date "2026-07-16" ;
      zoo:editor "Unknown editor" ;
      zoo:file "./zoo/zoo27/2e.xml" ;
      zoo:identifier "de_aucupio" ;
      zoo:title "De Aucupio" .


<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1/text/3>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 3 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "This account is not p514 free from suspicion, any more than certain points in the Latinity and prosody of the lines." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1/text/2>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 2 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "He records that they were surreptitiously copied by a young friend of his, Hieronymus Boragineus of Lübeck, from a poem De Aucupio by Nemesianus 'in bibliotheca porcorum (sic) Salvatoris Bononiensis.'" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "Gybertus Longolius (de Longueil, 1507‑1543), in a Dialogus de avibus printed at Cologne in 1544, is the authority for ascribing the two following fragments to Nemesianus." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1/text/6>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 6 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "E. Baehrens' text, P. L. M. III pp203‑204. J. P. Postgate's text, C. P. L. II p572. (p513)" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1/text/5>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 5 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "Teuffel considers the lines a late production, though they are usually printed along with the Cynegetica." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1/text/4>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 4 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "Contemplaverit in l. 3 may be an archaistic return to the active form of the verb as used in early Latin; but the metrical quantity of notae which Longolius read in l. 13 and of gulae in the last line of all is unclassical, and the frequent elision of a long vowel (ll. 5, 6, 14 and 27) is noticeable." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/9>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 9 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "It feeds close to the edge of embankments, by the wash of the water, hunting tiny worms, its favourite fare." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/7>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 7 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "When the woodland everywhere is despoiled of its green honours, make straight for the deep forest, mounted on the snow-white housing of your steed. The snipe is an easy and agreeable prey." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/8>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 8 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "You will find it no larger in body than Venus' doves." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/5>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 5 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "The guardian of the Tarpeian citadel⁠ is no larger in study, nor the bird that taught you, Palamedes, wing-like letters.⁠" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/6>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 6 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Often have I seen a slave swaying beneath the unfair weight of a huge dish of such dainties,⁠ as he carries the collation which a consul or a new praetor has furnished for the circus at a fête." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/3>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 3 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "For it is quick to shake off the treacherous bonds of the neck when caught, deriding⁠" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3> ;
      zoo:text "The Loeb Editor's Notes: 1 a black grouse. The bird is identified with the urogallus by Longolius. Pliny's form is tetras. Thayer's Note: 'Pliny's form' is a mystery. Our translators provide no citation; and I find no tetras (or tetrax or tarax) in any form anywhere in Pliny, either the most likely Elder or the marginally possible Younger; nor for that matter in Lewis & Short." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/4>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 4 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "in the joy of peace. Near Peltinum⁠ a by the foot of the Apennine range it builds its nest where the sun presents himself to the outspread lands: at the neck it is very like ashes in colour, and its spotted back is marked with dark flecks in the fashion of a partridge." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "I . . . and the tetrax ,⁠ It is far the silliest of birds; for although it has perched and was watched the snare laid for it, yet reckless of self it darts upon its own hurt." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/2>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 2 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "You, however, on finding the circles of the noose drawn tight, must hasten up and carry off your prey with its whirring wings." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3/text/4>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 4 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3> ;
      zoo:text "For the mazonomus ( μαζονόμος ) see Hor. Sat. II . VIII .86 ." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2/text/10>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 10 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "But its pursuit thereof is rather with keen-scented nose than with the eyes, in which its sense is rather dull, too big for the body though they be. With the point of the beak driven into the ground it drags out the little worms which needs must follow, therewith rewarding an appetite cheap to satisfy.⁠" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3/text/2>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 2 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3> ;
      zoo:text "geese of the Capitol saved it from surprise by the Gauls, in 390 B.C., Livy, V . XLVII ." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3/text/3>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 3 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/NEMESIANUS,_MARCUS_AURELIUS_OLYMPUS/de_aucupio/e/3> ;
      zoo:text "Palamedes was said to have invented some of the Greek letters ( Υ , Θ , Ξ , Φ , Χ ) by observing the flight of cranes: cf. Martial, of the Epigrams of Martial IX . XIII .7 , of the Epigrams of Martial XIII . LXXV ; Ausonius, Idyll. XII ( Technopaegnion de literis monosyllabis ) 25 Ausonius:TECHNOPAEGNION; Plin. N. H. VII .192 ." .


